 "question": "What does the recovered hideSubmitTab rule do for a single non-multi-select question, and how is it applied to the product grouped-question flow?",
 "answer": "hwe derives qr = questions.length===1 && !questions[0].multiSelect. That hides the submit tab, sets the next-tab bound to 0 so Right never opens the review page, and the answer handler submits the whole request as soon as a non-array answer is taken. The product derives the same condition from groups.length===1 && !group.multiple: advanceDialog records the group answer and finishes immediately, and the review Right branch is inert.",
